# ============================================================================
# Stock_Prediction_app_push — repository root .gitignore
# ============================================================================
# Phase 5-G1B — Raw provider-payload cache hygiene.
#
# PURPOSE
#   Future raw provider response payloads written by the controlled collectors
#   (most importantly the Phase 3-M Alpha Vantage earnings collector run with
#   --live) must be ignored by Git by default, so a newly collected raw payload
#   can NEVER be accidentally staged or committed.
#
# EXISTING HISTORY (important)
#   Some historical raw payloads were committed BEFORE this rule existed and
#   remain TRACKED — e.g. the 50 Alpha Vantage earnings JSON files already in
#   research/output/phase3m_earnings_estimates_signal_gate/raw/. A .gitignore
#   rule does NOT untrack files already in the index, and Phase 5-G1B does not
#   untrack them: they are intentionally left in place. They are factual EPS
#   estimate / actual / surprise numbers (committed-safe, no secrets, no keys).
#   This rule only prevents NEW raw payloads from being staged going forward.
#
# WHAT STAYS ALLOWED (NOT ignored)
#   Committed-safe summary artifacts — coverage / quality / manifest CSVs and
#   JSON (row counts, redacted URLs, file paths; never payloads or API keys)
#   under research/output/<phase>/ — remain tracked. Only the per-provider
#   raw/ payload directories below are ignored.
# ============================================================================

# --- Phase 3-M earnings collector raw Alpha Vantage payloads (explicit target) ---
research/output/phase3m_earnings_estimates_signal_gate/raw/

# --- Belt-and-braces: any per-provider raw payload directory under research/output ---
# Gitignore '*' does not cross '/', so this matches only research/output/<phase>/raw/
# payload dirs. Committed-safe summary artifacts live one level up and are unaffected.
research/output/*/raw/
